From 393a6a7f960880d4924e67a2cef7482bd18060d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Audit <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:03:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Audit fixes: link previews, LocalBusiness schema,
 review-submit race, rate limit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five fixes from the end-to-end audit. No behaviour change for existing
users; each is either a correctness fix or metadata that was absent.

1. LINK PREVIEWS WERE BLANK EVERYWHERE. No og:image was set, so every
   share on Facebook, WhatsApp and LinkedIn rendered with no picture, and
   og:url was hardcoded to the homepage — a shared /services link claimed
   to be the front page. metadataBase lets Next derive og:url and a
   canonical per page; twitter:card moves to summary_large_image.

2. NO STRUCTURED DATA. For a local trade the map pack is where the calls
   come from, and there was no JSON-LD at all. Adds LocalBusiness with
   address, service area, phone and hours. Hours are Mon-Fri 07:00-17:00
   to match CLOSED_DAY_INDICES; if the contact page's Saturday hours are
   correct then BOTH need changing together, plus the Google profile.
   aggregateRating is deliberately omitted — Google requires ratings to
   be really collected and shown on the page, and inventing one risks a
   manual action.

3. THE REVIEW 409 WAS ADVISORY, NOT ENFORCED. The responded_at check and
   the UPDATE were separate statements, so two submissions racing on one
   token both passed the check and both wrote. Conditioning the UPDATE on
    lets the database pick the winner; .select()
   distinguishes a real claim from a loser, since Supabase reports success
   either way. Newly relevant — the table only started existing today.

4. THE ONLY UNMETERED PUBLIC WRITE. The other three public endpoints rate
   limit; this one didn't. Not about guessing a 128-bit token, about not
   leaving an unauthenticated write path open to hammering. 10 per 10 min
   so a customer who mis-taps and retries is never blocked.

5. "Now in 2025" on the About page, read in August 2026. Dropped the year
   rather than bumping it, so it can't go stale again.

Deliberately NOT changed: HIRE_PUBLIC_LAUNCH. The hero's "Coming soon"
tile is that flag, not an oversight — flipping it launches the hire
product publicly, which is Thomas's call and not an audit fix.

Verified: tsc --noEmit passes with zero errors. next build fails only on
next/font reaching fonts.googleapis.com, which this sandbox blocks; the
failing file (src/app/hire/layout.tsx) is untouched by this commit.
