From e8703789ea970cf4dc60a3b1f7843b9a9c6a2d6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Audit <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 02:11:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Doug enquiries now push to admins; add a database backup
 script
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TWO SEPARATE THINGS, both surfaced by testing the live site today.

DOUG CAPTURES WERE EMAIL-ONLY. The contact form notifies admins twice —
push and email — on the reasoning, written in its own comments, that the
email lands 'even if the OneSignal push misses or his phone is off'. Doug
had only the email half. Proven by submitting one lead through each route
and reading the runtime logs: /api/enquiries attempted both, /api/enquiry
attempted only the email. With Resend still unverified that meant a lead
arriving through the chatbot reached nobody at all — it sat in the table
until someone happened to open the admin console.

The push is fired best-effort and unawaited: Doug is a live conversation,
so the customer must not wait on OneSignal, and a failed push must not
stop the email that follows it. Deep-links to the job when the capture
converted to one, else the enquiry, else the list.

BACKUP SCRIPT. The schema was never at risk — 39 migrations in git rebuild
it exactly. The data was, and is: free-plan Supabase has no point-in-time
recovery, so 325 jobs, 41 clients, leave balances and paid hours have no
recovery path at all. A migration already sat unapplied for three weeks
without anyone noticing, which is the same blind spot in a different form.

xero_tokens is excluded from the data dump deliberately. Those rows are
live OAuth refresh tokens, and a backup that gets copied to a laptop or a
cloud drive would turn one file into a credential leak. Xero reconnects
through OAuth after a restore, so nothing is actually lost.

Storage buckets are NOT covered — job photos, hire photos and flyers live
in Supabase Storage, which pg_dump cannot see. That gap is real and still
open; this script does not pretend otherwise.

backups/ and *.sql.gz added to .gitignore so a dump full of customer names,
addresses and payroll data can never be committed by accident.

Verified: tsc --noEmit passes; bash -n on the script passes.
---
