Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Lawn mowing enquiries stop arriving labelled Garden
 Maintenance
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Lawn mowing & edging" is the first item in the canonical SERVICES list
and the most common job Thomas does, but it was missing from
SERVICE_OPTIONS — the list the contact form's dropdown is built from and
the one ?service= is validated against.

Both links that advertise it therefore fell back to the nearest existing
option, Garden Maintenance: the footer's Services column and the first
tile on /services. A customer clicking "Lawn mowing & edging" landed on a
form already filled in as something else, and the enquiry reached Thomas
under the wrong heading. He could still work it out by reading the
message, but the label is what he sorts and prices by, so a mow request
and a full maintenance visit were indistinguishable at a glance.

Adding the option fixes both links at their source rather than patching
each one, since the type is derived from the array — a future link that
names a service not on the list still fails the same way, which is the
intended behaviour and is what surfaced this.

Placed first in the array to match the canonical order used on the
homepage cards, /services tiles and footer.

Verified: tsc --noEmit passes.
